# ── notebook generator (plot URL → JupyterLite-compatible .ipynb) ────────────
#
# Anthive-web wants an "open this plot in a notebook" button on every plot
# page. This endpoint takes the EXACT same query-param surface as
# /plot/{geom} and returns a 3-cell .ipynb (markdown + two code cells)
# that:
#   1) introduces the plot with the same X-Plot-Caption the image carries,
#   2) re-fetches the plot's source dataframe as CSV (DataFrame ready),
#   3) renders the PNG inline with the caption underneath.
#
# Auth-block is templated at render time:
#   - Authelia / Remote-User present → Case B (user known, active line uses
#     the JupyterLite-origin cookie; explicit-password line commented).
#   - HTTP Basic credentials present → Case C with username pre-filled.
#   - ANTHIVE_PUBLIC=1 env var → Case A (passwordless; no auth at all).
#   - Otherwise → Case C with <user>/<password> placeholders.
#
# BASE_URL inside the notebook is derived from X-Forwarded-Host (Caddy)
# falling back to the Host header so the notebook is portable across
# deployments.

# Mapping from the user-facing query param names declared by the per-geom
# /plot/{geom} endpoints to the kwarg names _build_plot_request() expects.
# Anything not in this dict is forwarded with its query-param name unchanged.
